{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.KnotTheory","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.no_isolated_quark_in_borromean_baryon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.no_isolated_quark_in_borromean_baryon","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L117-L123","doc":"Decategorified corollary used by\n`rem:borromean-topological-confinement`: no isolated quark\ncan survive the removal-of-one-component operation on a\nBorromean baryon, because the remaining link is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.borromean_brunnian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.borromean_brunnian","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L98-L115","doc":"**Brunnian property of the Borromean rings** (conditional on\n`LinkEquivalence`).  Removing any of the three components of\n`𝓑₃` yields a two-component sub-link whose closure is the\ntrivial unlink `U₂`.\n\nNaive deletion at the BraidWord level does not literally\nyield the empty braid: for `i = 0` we get\n`(σ₀⁻¹)³ ∈ B₂`, whose closure is the negative trefoil; the\ndischarge to `U₂` is by an R3-then-R2-twice sequence, which\nis precisely the content of the `LinkEquivalence` class.\n\n-- Ref: [kawauchi1996] Survey of Knot Theory §1.5\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:brunnian-property-of-borromean\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:brunnian-property-of-borromean","label":"conj:brunnian-property-of-borromean","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/brunnian-property-of-borromean.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.LinkEquivalence.brunnian_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.LinkEquivalence.brunnian_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.LinkEquivalence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.LinkEquivalence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.LinkEquivalence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.LinkEquivalence","kind":"class","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L86-L96","doc":"**§3b-cond conjectural witness.**  Discharging this class\ninstance is equivalent to formalising the link-equivalence\nrelation on braid-word closures — i.e. proving that two\nbraid words present the same link iff they are related by a\nfinite sequence of Reidemeister moves (R1/R2/R3) and Markov\nmoves (conjugation + stabilisation).\n\n-- Ref: [leitner2026] conj:brunnian-property-of-borromean\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.isUnlink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.isUnlink","kind":"opaque","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L73-L84","doc":"`isUnlink β` asserts that the Markov closure of `β` is the\ntrivial `β.components`-component unlink.\n\nDeclared `opaque` because the full predicate needs the\nReidemeister + Markov equivalence relation on braid-word\nclosures, which is not yet formalised in Mathlib.  The\nconjectural-class hypothesis `[LinkEquivalence]` below\nplays the role of an explicit witness.\n\n-- Ref: [kawauchi1996] Survey of Knot Theory §1.2\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.BraidWord.deleteComponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.BraidWord.deleteComponent","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L64-L71","doc":"Naive component deletion on a braid word: drops the strand\nat position `i` and renumbers higher generators.  See the\n`deleteLetters` doc-comment for the topological caveat. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.deleteLetters","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.KnotTheory.Brunnian.deleteLetters","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/KnotTheory/Brunnian.lean#L45-L62","doc":"Naive strand-deletion on a list of braid letters.  Drops\nevery letter whose generator touches strand `i` (index\n`i-1` or `i`), and decrements the index of every surviving\nletter whose index `> i` so the result is well-typed for\n`B_{n-1}`.\n\nTopologically this preserves the link only modulo the\nReidemeister + Markov equivalence relation; recovering the\nactual sub-link requires the as-yet-unformalised\nlink-equivalence machinery. ","signatureChunk":0}]}